<GuideLayout 
  title="Eco-Performance: Sustainable Fabrics in Activewear Manufacturing"
  type="SUSTAINABILITY"
  description="Explore the future of athletic apparel. Balancing high-performance compression with eco-friendly recycled materials."
>
  <p>Sustainability is no longer a niche requirement; it is a global consumer expectation. At FITCLO, we are bridging the gap between recycled materials and professional-grade athletic support, ensuring your brand stands on the cutting edge of innovation.</p>
  
  <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 my-10 text-center">
    <div class="p-8 bg-green-50 rounded-2xl border border-green-100">
      <h4 class="font-bold text-green-800 mb-2">Recycled Nylon</h4>
      <p class="text-xs text-green-700/70">Repurposed from fishing nets and pre-consumer waste.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="p-8 bg-green-50 rounded-2xl border border-green-100">
      <h4 class="font-bold text-green-800 mb-2">rPET (Recycled Poly)</h4>
      <p class="text-xs text-green-700/70">Diverting plastic bottles from oceans into durable gear.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="p-8 bg-green-50 rounded-2xl border border-green-100">
      <h4 class="font-bold text-green-800 mb-2">Bio-Based Spandex</h4>
      <p class="text-xs text-green-700/70">Elastic fibers derived from renewable corn sources.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Certifications Matter: GRS & OEKO-TEX</h2>
  <p>We provide full traceability for our eco-fabrics, including <strong>Global Recycled Standard (GRS)</strong> and <strong>OEKO-TEX Standard 100</strong>. This transparency allows your brand to market "Sustainable" collections with verified claims that resonate with conscious consumers.</p>

  <h2>Performance Testing: Eco-Fabrics vs. Virgin Nylon</h2>
  <p>The short answer: <strong>Modern recycled fabrics match virgin performance.</strong> In our lab tests, recycled Nylon-66 provides the same tensile strength and "hand-feel" as traditional fabrics. Professional athletes cannot distinguish the difference in compression or sweat-wicking ability.</p>

  <p><em>Building a greener brand? Download our 2026 Sustainable Fabric Catalog to see our full range of GRS-certified options and start your eco-collection today.</em></p>
</GuideLayout>
